LT + password), hex-encoded lowercase.\\n    - Example: echo -n \"somesaltpassword\" | sha256sum | awk \\'{print $1}\\'\\n  - Update EXPECTED_PWHASH in /workspace/login.c.\\n\\nNotes\\n- This is a safe, minimal prototype.\\n- For production, switch to a KDF (argon2/scrypt/bcrypt/PBKDF2), per-user salts, and a proper credential store.\\n\\nIf you want me to switch to a built-in SHA-256 implementation (removing OpenSSL dependency), or to rename the binary/file further (e.g., /workspace/login), I can do that next.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(content='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\\nIf you want to give up, run: <execute_bash> exit </execute_bash>.\\n', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action='message', security_risk=None), RecallAction(recall_type='knowledge', query='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\\nIf you want to give up, run: <execute_bash> exit </execute_bash>.\\n', thought='', action='recall'), CmdRunAction(command='bash -lc \"set -e; gcc -std=c11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -o /workspace/login /workspace/login.c -lcrypto; printf \\'TEST1 valid -> \\'; printf \\'user\\\\npassword\\\\n\\' | /workspace/login >/dev/null; echo rc=$?; printf \\'TEST2 invalid -> \\'; printf \\'user\\\\nwrong\\\\n\\' | /workspace/login >/dev/null; echo rc=$?; printf \\'TEST3 valid capture -> \\'; printf \\'user\\\\npassword\\\\n\\' | /workspace/login; echo CAPTURED_RC:$?; printf \\'TEST4 invalid capture -> \\'; printf \\'user\\\\nwrong\\\\n\\' | /workspace/login; echo CAPTURED_RC:$?\"', is_input=False, thought='', blocking=False, hidden=False, action='run', confirmation_state='confirmed'